TYPES.md §7.4, §15, DECISIONS 444: a default reading a field of a record literal is checked as the literal it folds to, at the default, whether the literal leaves the field out or gives it, its record declared later: two E3204, and no value takes either default.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record U {
  x: Int(1..3) = (T {}).a
  y: Int(1..) = (T { b: 0 }).b
}

local record T {
  a: Int = 5
  b: Int = 1
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3204]  a/a.canon:4:18
  5 is outside 1..3
  expected by a/a.canon:4 (x: Int(1..3))

error[E3204]  a/a.canon:5:17
  0 is outside 1..
  expected by a/a.canon:5 (y: Int(1..))

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
